1.14.0 Release notes (2026-09-29)
================================

Improvements to the 'RingPublishingTracking' module.

### Changes

* Session identifier ("IS") is now available to the host application
    - new 'sessionIdentifier' field of the public 'TrackingIdentifier' model, delivered with 'didAssignTrackingIdentifier'
    - new 'didAssignSessionIdentifier' method of 'RingPublishingTrackingDelegate', called during 'initialize', before the backend identifiers are fetched
    - both deliver the same value, which is also the 'IS' reported with every event, so it is not replaced once the backend identifiers arrive
    - the new delegate method has a default empty implementation, existing delegates keep compiling
* View type of the 'RDLC' parameter moved out of the 'client' object
    - reported as top level 'view' object next to 'client' and 'variant', carrying the value under 'type' (e.g. {"view":{"type":"text"}}), instead of 'client.viewType' introduced in 1.13.0
    - public API is unchanged, 'viewType' of 'reportContentPageView' works as before
    - events reported without a view type still omit the key
* Events reported while the tracking identifiers are fetched now wait for them
    - on a fresh install the first events (e.g. the first page view) were sent before the identify request finished, without 'eaUUID' in 'ids', so the backend recorded them without 'lu'
    - such events are now sent once the identity request in flight finishes; when it fails they are still sent, as before
    - the Artemis identifier in 'RDLU' is still taken when the event is reported, so the very first event of a fresh install can still go out without it
* Identity is requested again after a failed identify request
    - a failed first identify request left the SDK without identifiers for the rest of the session, it is now retried when events are sent, at most once every 30 seconds
* Events reported after a relaunch, before the Artemis identifier is fetched again, carry the still valid identifier stored by the previous session
